    "id": "matroid_rank3_bounded_parallel_basis_floor",
    "title": "Rank-three matroids with bounded parallel classes have many bases",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "deletion-contraction at a smallest parallel class",
    "statement": "Let M be a loopless rank-three matroid on m elements whose parallel classes have size at most a. Then 2b(M)>=(m-1)(m-1-a). If a divides m-1 and m-1>=2a, equality is attained by one coloop over a rank-two matroid whose parallel classes all have size a.",
